v 3
d gepwreg. Percentile Weights Regression with analytical standard errors
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar
d Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260619
d
d Description:
d gepwreg estimates the Percentile Weights Regression (PWR) of Araar
d (2016, 2023): the local marginal effect of the regressors on the outcome
d for observations whose rank in the distribution of the outcome (or of
d another ranking variable) is in the neighbourhood of a target percentile.
d Version 1.3 implements the results of Araar (2026): closed-form analytical
d standard errors by linearisation, which account for the estimation of the
d kernel weights; an MSE-optimal bandwidth chosen by a two-step plug-in rule;
d Taylor linearisation under a complex survey design declared by svyset; a
d pairs bootstrap that re-estimates the weights at each replication; and
d ranking on any variable other than the outcome.  A dialog box is included.
d
d This is the version of June 2026, kept so that results published with it
d can be reproduced.  It is superseded by version 1.4, which replaces the
d outcome-ranked estimator by a two-step estimator of the effect at a
d quantile; see the repository README before using 1.3 for new work.
d
d bkf98I.dta, retrieved by net get, is the Burkina Faso 1998 household
d survey extract used in the paper and in the help file examples.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
f gepwreg.ado
f gepwreg.sthlp
f gepwreg.dlg
f bkf98I.dta
